# OMN-13437 / OMN-13418 Phase 2a: un-forgeable prod-promotion trust anchor.
# This file is the canonical grant registry. Platform leads are the intended
# reviewers of any change to it, but this CODEOWNERS entry is ADVISORY, not
# enforced: `required_pull_request_reviews` is intentionally NOT enabled on
# `dev` (enabling it would block a platform-lead-authored grant PR from ever
# being approvable, since GitHub rejects self-approval of your own PR — see
# feedback_no_approval_required).
#
# CODEOWNERS review (advisory, as stated above) is currently the ONLY
# defense this repo offers against a self-approved prod-promotion grant
# entering `grants/prod_promotion_grants.yaml`. It is not backed by a
# mechanical check: `validate-prod-promotion-grants`
# (src/onex_change_control/scripts/validate_prod_promotion_grants.py) governs
# schema/integrity only — required fields, digest format, unique grant_id,
# freshness, `entries: []` at rest. Its earlier `approved_by != PR-author`
# self-approval check (OMN-14441) was removed by OMN-14814 (solo CODEOWNER
# made a second-approver requirement unsatisfiable) and nothing in this repo
# replaced it. Reinstating a mechanical approver != requester control is
# tracked in OMN-17157, gated on OMN-14445 (CODEOWNERS review on `dev` is
# itself unenforced) closing first.
#
# The surviving self-approval control on any live prod promotion is
# `approved_by != requested_by`, enforced by the omninode_infra dispatch
# gate (`omninode_infra/scripts/validate_prod_promotion_grant.py`, wired
# into `deploy-onex-prod.yml`) — not by anything in this repo. Do not read
# this file's checks as covering that case.
#
# `check-platform-leads-review-tripwire` (OMN-14445) still runs, but its
# original premise — that OMN-14441's check was a complete defense only
# while platform-leads has exactly one member — no longer applies: that
# check is gone regardless of team size, so the tripwire's pass/fail no
# longer signals anything about self-approval coverage here. OMN-14445
# remains open to decide the CODEOWNERS-enforcement question the tripwire
# was standing in for.
grants/prod_promotion_grants.yaml @OmniNode-ai/platform-leads

# OMN-16702: PUBLIC-cluster staging-class namespace authorization anchor.
# Same ADVISORY status as the prod anchor above — `required_pull_request_reviews`
# is intentionally NOT enabled on `dev`, so this line does not mechanically
# block anything. Stated plainly so it is not mistaken for enforcement: the
# mechanical defenses on THIS anchor are scope-narrowing, not approver-
# authentication. `validate-staging-namespace-grants` (ci.yml) pins scope,
# runtime_lane, cluster and the {dev, onex-dev} namespace allowlist fail-closed,
